+/*
+ * Scaled text console for the boot menu and Super Fastboot screens.
+ *
+ * nx809j local change. Every Canoe screen is printed through gST->ConOut, and
+ * the firmware console draws its 8x19 font 1:1: about 150 columns of tiny text
+ * on a 1216x2688 panel. This console implements the same protocol on top of
+ * GOP, drawing the EDK2 standard glyphs at an integer scale chosen so that a
+ * row holds at least SFB_BIG_MIN_COLUMNS characters. QueryMode reports the
+ * smaller grid, so the menu geometry code lays itself out for it unchanged.
+ *
+ * The highlighted row (black on light gray) is drawn white on an accent
+ * color instead.
+ *
+ * Text written here is not forwarded to the firmware console: it would draw
+ * the small text over the large one. Menu text therefore no longer reaches the
+ * firmware's serial ring; the SFB: MARK lines still do.
+ *
+ * Glyph bitmaps: MdeModulePkg/Universal/Console/GraphicsConsoleDxe/LaffStd.c
+ * (Copyright (c) 2006 - 2008, Intel Corporation, BSD-2-Clause-Patent),
+ * code points 0x20-0x7e.
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+ */
